159
00:15:36,950 --> 00:15:42,710
Others are much larger structures that soar up to 40 meters into the cold air.

160
00:15:42,990 --> 00:15:47,370
Most consist of timber frames that rest on stone blocks.

161
00:15:47,950 --> 00:15:51,190
This means that they have no foundations.

162
00:15:51,870 --> 00:15:56,750
Although many of the churches appear from the outside to be complex structures, they

163
00:15:56,750 --> 00:16:02,370
normally feature only a single story, but numerous different roof levels.

164
00:16:03,470 --> 00:16:08,870
Staff from the Norwegian government have carried out conservation work on 10 of the

165
00:16:08,870 --> 00:16:10,790
churches over the past two years.

166
00:16:11,630 --> 00:16:15,850
Most of these churches date from between the 12th and 14th centuries.

167
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:19,570
Other churches were conserved in previous years.

168
00:16:19,570 --> 00:16:25,190
So far, specialists have worked to add preservative materials to the church's

169
00:16:25,190 --> 00:16:31,430
exteriors. They also replaced rotting roofs and halted the sinking of the churches

170
00:16:31,430 --> 00:16:32,410
into the ground.

171
00:16:33,350 --> 00:16:39,030
In two cases, huge machines have been used to lift the buildings up to 30

172
00:16:39,030 --> 00:16:40,930
centimeters into the air.

173
00:16:41,370 --> 00:16:46,150
This was accomplished so that the could examine and repair the church's original

174
00:16:46,150 --> 00:16:47,870
medieval stone blocks.

175
00:16:47,870 --> 00:16:53,710
The team plans to return to around a dozen of the buildings to assess progress and

176
00:16:53,710 --> 00:16:55,330
